</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Canberra, NPHP</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Alliance for Health Policy and Systems Research</collab></person-group><article-title>Getting research into policy and practice</article-title><source>Strengthening health systems: the promise of policy and systems research</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Geneva, Alliance for Health Policy and Systems Research</publisher-name><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>70</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Lomas J</collab></person-group><source>Improving research dissemination and uptake in the health sector: beyond the sound of one hand clapping</source><year>1997</year><publisher-name>Hamilton, Ont., McMaster University Centre for Health Economics and Policy Analysis</publisher-name><fpage>42</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Walter I</collab><collab>Davies H</collab><collab>Nutley S</collab></person-group><article-title>Increasing research impact through partnerships: Evidence from outside health care</article-title><source>J Health Serv Res Policy</source><year>2003</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>58</fpage><lpage>61</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14596749</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1258/135581903322405180</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Sauerborn R</collab><collab>Nitayarumphong S</collab><collab>Gerhardus A</collab></person-group><article-title>Strategies to enhance the use of health systems research for health system reform</article-title><source>Trop Med Int Health</source><year>1999</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>827</fpage><lpage>835</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10632991</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1